   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Talking about the future",
     "texto": [
      "**Skal + infinitive** expresses a plan: **Jeg skal flytte** («I'm going to move»). After **skal** there is no **å**, unlike English «going to move». **Vil + infinitive** expresses will or intention: **Jeg vil begynne** («I want to / I'm going to start»).",
      "Norwegian can use the same form to talk about the future that English expresses with «going to» or with the present; the context shows whether it is a plan or an intention."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Talking about goals",
     "texto": [
      "**Planlegger å + infinitive** means «I plan to…». **Ønsker å + infinitive** means «I want to…» or «I wish to…». In Spanish «que + subjunctive» is sometimes used; in Norwegian the infinitive with **å** follows, as in English «I want to…»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
